  },
  "holistic_F_N": 2,
  "holistic_F_H": 1,
  "section_notes": "The final v25 text sets a 7% permanent per-model failure ceiling for S2 with no transition and no existing-model exemption, which is well above the 5% discussed and keeps Northwind's Hearth 10 (6.2%) on sale. S5 keeps a model-specific mandatory recall above 8 per 100k but adds a regulator-approved, time-limited corrective-action alternative with no stated duration, which creates a route for Halcyon's Ember 8 (9.9) to avoid recall. S1 is strong (24-hour reporting of all thermal incidents, retroactive disclosure of prior unreported incidents), while S3 (new units at 24 months, retrofit at 72) and S4 (suppression at 36 months) sit in the middle of the discussed ranges."
 },
